---
title: Diagrama de clases final (después de refactorizar)
---
classDiagram
    direction TB

    class BaseModel {
        <<pydantic>>
    }
    class FastAPI {
        <<FastAPI>>
        +state.database: Database
    }
    class HTTPException {
        <<FastAPI>>
        +status_code: int
        +detail: str
    }
    class Connection {
        <<sqlite3>>
    }

    class Database {
        +path: str
        +connect() Iterator~Connection~
        +initialize() None
    }

    class ProductInput {
        +name: str
        +price_cents: int
        +stock: int
    }
    class CustomerInput {
        +name: str
        +email: EmailStr
        +category: Literal["regular", "premium", "business"]
    }
    class ItemInput {
        +product_id: int
        +quantity: int
    }
    class OrderInput {
        +customer_id: int
        +address: str
        +city: str
        +postal_code: str
        +shipping: Literal["pickup", "standard", "express"]
        +items: list~ItemInput~
        +unique_products() OrderInput
    }

    class OrderService {
        +database: Database
        +quote(data: OrderInput) dict
        +create(data: OrderInput) dict
        +update(order_id, data: OrderInput) dict
        +get(order_id) dict
        +list() list~dict~
        +confirm(order_id) dict
        +cancel(order_id) dict
        +delete(order_id) None
        +notifications(order_id) list~dict~
        -_price(connection, data: OrderInput) tuple
        -_order_values(data: OrderInput, category, totals)$ tuple
        -_insert_lines(connection, order_id, lines)$ None
        -_find_order(connection, order_id)$ Row
        -_find_pending(connection, order_id, conflict_message) Row
        -_detail(connection, order_id) dict
    }

    BaseModel <|-- ProductInput
    BaseModel <|-- CustomerInput
    BaseModel <|-- ItemInput
    BaseModel <|-- OrderInput
    OrderInput *-- "1..100" ItemInput : items

    FastAPI --> "1" Database : state.database
    OrderService --> "1" Database : database
    Database ..> Connection : abre y confirma
    OrderService ..> Connection : SQL sobre 5 tablas
    OrderService ..> OrderInput : quote / create / update(data)
    OrderService ..> HTTPException : lanza 404 / 409

    note for OrderService "_price() usa la función de módulo calculate_totals(category, shipping, subtotal)<br>y las constantes DISCOUNT_PERCENT, FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS, STANDARD_SHIPPING_CENTS,<br>EXPRESS_SHIPPING_CENTS, PENDING, CONFIRMED y CANCELLED (app/orders.py; no son clases).<br>SQL sobre orders, order_items, customers, products y notifications."
    note for Database "Las rutas de app/products.py y app/customers.py<br>usan Database directamente (no hay clase de servicio)."
